      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T20:27:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When these return cases are hit, createAccessor will call generate, and since sockaddr is not modified, it doesn\u0027t know there is a failure, so it would try to use the unmodified sockaddr. If a sockaddr is re-used, that could lead to it making a connection to something else. \u0027generator\u0027 here should return that it failed, so that createAccessor can fail (and either return an error or return nullptr).\n\n\u003e change the behavior of libbinder/libbinder_ndk based on what a user\u0027s callback is telling us outside of a OK(non-null)/Not OK(null)\n\n+1, binary info is okay. It\u0027s nice if we can return more detailed error for debugging, but the main thing that\u0027s needed is knowing when we failed.\n\n\u003e Unsupported address/socket types (this highlighted line) - libbinder already handles this\n\nerr, yeah, so I think it\u0027s impossible for it to handle this, given the current implementation of generator. Am I missing something?",
